{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgac6pHnwMRTAsCpjoRTQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I replaced the `sorry` in `Main.lean` with a proof, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem times_eq_mul (n m : Nat) : times n m = n * m := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero => simp [times]\n  | succ k ih => simp [times, ih, Nat.succ_mul]\n```\n\nThe proof works by induction on `n`:\n- **Base case (`n = 0`):** `times 0 m` is defined as `0`, and `0 * m = 0`, so `simp` closes it.\n- **Step (`n = k + 1`):** `times (k+1) m` unfolds to `times k m + m`. The induction hypothesis turns that into `k * m + m`, and `Nat.succ_mul` shows this equals `(k+1) * m`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":415,"cache_read_input_tokens":7853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":415},"output_tokens":274,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2b2fc8b-6c38-4610-95f4-68d418de77eb","uuid":"3d5383e6-ca87-460d-9a4e-df435393c0f7","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:09:49.210Z","request_id":"req_011Cgac6p3uKTS8i4rkuW28g"}
